    "result_text": "I investigated thoroughly and the specification is **already fully satisfied** by the code in the repository \u2014 no source change is needed, which is also the lowest possible structural impact (zero functions/files touched).\n\n## What I verified\n\n**All rejection paths for 400 / 409 / 429 already emit RFC7807 `application/problem+json`.** Every escalation handler for an in-scope status builds its body through a single shared helper, `ProblemDetails.build(...)`, which sets all four required members:\n\n- `type` \u2192 `about:blank`\n- `title` \u2192 exception simple name\n- `status` \u2192 from `ProblemDetail.forStatus(status)`\n- `detail` \u2192 the message\n\nand responds via `ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>>`, which serializes with the `application/problem+json` content type and preserves the HTTP status.\n\nCoverage by status (all wired in `officefloor/escalation/*.yml`):\n- **400** \u2014 `ValidationExceptionHandler`, `InvalidAddress/Postcode/Telephone`, `DisposableEmail`, `RegistrationDateInFuture`\n- **409** \u2014 `CityAtCapacity`, `DuplicateEmail/Household/Identity/Telephone`\n- **429** \u2014 `DailyRegistrationLimit`\n\nI also confirmed there are **no rejection responses built outside the escalation handlers** (grep for `BAD_REQUEST`/`CONFLICT`/`TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`/`badRequest`/`status(4\u2026)` outside `/escalation/` returned nothing), so there's no bypass path returning a plain body. `NotFound` (404) and `Forbidden` (403) are out of scope and unchanged.\n\n## Test evidence\n\n- The provided new test `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` (400, asserts `application/problem+json` + `$.status == 400`) **passes**.\n- To confirm the mechanism generalizes to a non-400 status, I added a throwaway test exercising the duplicate (409) path asserting `type`/`title`/`status==409`/`detail` and the content type \u2014 it passed \u2014 then removed it.\n- Full suite after cleanup: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test, 0 failures.\n\nThe change described is already in place and green; I made no modifications to the application.",
